// The workloads whose e2e scenario has actually booted them on a live cluster, and
// the date it last did. This is the evidence behind the `e2e` maturity tier: a
// scenario merely existing proves nothing, so gen-maturity grants the tier only to
// the workloads listed here.
//
// A workload is added when its scenario is observed green — by the e2e pipeline on
// a real cluster, or by a maintainer running `hack/smoke/scenario-<id>.sh` against
// one. Remove a workload if its scenario starts failing; the tier must never claim
// more than the run proves.
